# Optional TURN relay for online play across different networks
# (for example a phone on mobile data and a laptop on Wi-Fi).
#
# These are server-side only: they are read by the /api/turn function
# (api/turn.ts) and never compiled into the browser bundle.
#
# Production: add them in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# (mark as Sensitive), then redeploy.
# Local: copy this file to .env.local. `npm run dev` serves /api/turn too.

# Option A: a credentials URL (Metered's free TURN plan provides one).
# TURN_CREDENTIALS_URL=https://<your-app>.metered.live/api/v1/turn/credentials?apiKey=<your-key>

# Option B: static TURN credentials.
# TURN_URLS=turn:relay.example.com:80,turn:relay.example.com:443?transport=tcp,turns:relay.example.com:443
# TURN_USERNAME=
# TURN_CREDENTIAL=
